<title>GERMANY: BASF says buys UK vitamin premix company.</title>
<headline>BASF says buys UK vitamin premix company.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>BASF plc, a subsidiary of German chemical giant BASF AG, said on Monday it had bought the UK vitamin premix and mineral feed company Frank Wright Ltd for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Frank Wright Ltd produces and sells vitamin premixes and mineral feeds mainly for the UK's compound feed market, which has a volume of around 20 million tonnes, BASF said in a statement.</p>
<p>Frank Wright has 150 employees and is based in Ashbourne, BASF said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
